---
/* One section of a people page, wearing the one heading and the one anchor the
 * spec gives it.
 *
 * Eight archives gave roughly the same content eight sets of names — «What the
 * registers say», «What the record says», «What is recorded», «The record», «What
 * is known», «What the archive knows», «Events, as the record has them». Measured on the built sites (13 October
 * 2026) only three headings are used by more than two archives: «Family» (Blazevic,
 * D'Arcy, Luwinski), «Where this comes from» (Falco, Lerena, Mazza) and «Others of
 * the same name» (Falco, Blazevic, Mazza), and none by more than three. A reader
 * who learns one archive's page has learned nothing about the next, and a link
 * to «the sources of this person» cannot be written once.
 *
 * So `kind` picks the heading and the id from lib/person.js PERSON_SECTIONS, and
 * a page cannot spell them differently by accident:
 *
 *   family     #family      Family                    required
 *   record     #record      What the record says      required
 *   sources    #sources     Where this comes from     required
 *   namesakes  #namesakes   Others of the same name   optional
 *   media      #media       Photographs and papers    optional
 *   notes      #notes       Notes and corrections     optional
 *
 * An archive with something the spec has no section for (Booyzen's household
 * panels, Mazza's «The crossing») passes `kind="more"` and a `title`: it is drawn,
 * after the six, with a class that says it is local, and checkperson.py counts it.
 * That is the honest place for it: not forbidden, not pretending to be shared.
 *
 * PROPS  kind   one of the six ids, or "more"
 *        title  only for kind="more"
 *        level  heading level, default 2 (the h1 is the page's)
 */
import { SECTION_BY_ID } from "../lib/person.js";
const { kind = "more", title = "", level = 2 } = Astro.props;
const known = SECTION_BY_ID[kind];
const heading = known ? known.heading : title || "More";
const id = known ? known.id : "more-" + String(title).toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "-").replace(/^-|-$/g, "");
const H = `h${Math.min(Math.max(Number(level) || 2, 2), 4)}`;
---
<section class={"psec" + (known ? "" : " psec-local")} id={id} aria-labelledby={id + "-h"} data-section={known ? kind : "more"}>
  <H class="psec-h" id={id + "-h"}>{heading}</H>
  <slot />
</section>
